Chapter: EffectHandlerNestedSame
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Semantics-pinning probe (effect rows stage 0). Nested handlers
 for the SAME effect: the innermost handler wins and discharges the
 perform completely (set semantics -- filter-effect removes every
 occurrence; rows keep this by idempotence). inner-value must be 10,
 not 99. Must compile and produce identical output today and under
 rows; if scoped-label semantics ever changes handler nesting, this
 probe is the tripwire.

Section: Effects

  effect Reader where
    ask : [Reader] Integer

Section: Definitions

  inner-value : Integer
  inner-value =
   let r = with Reader ask
     ask (resume) = resume 10
   in r

  outer-value : Integer
  outer-value =
   let r = with Reader inner-value
     ask (resume) = resume 99
   in r

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("inner " & show inner-value)
    print-line-uni ("outer " & show outer-value)
  end
